    "pressure": {
      "file": "mixed_bed_polisher_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Thousands of tiny demineralisers in series",
      "description": "In service the cation and anion beads are mixed, so the water meets alternate H⁺ and OH⁻ exchange sites thousands of times — like countless two-bed units in series. This \"polishes\" water to very high purity (conductivity < ~ 0.1 µS/cm, silica < ~ 10–20 µg/L) for high-pressure boilers and electronics. For regeneration the resins are separated by backwashing (lighter anion on top), regenerated separately, then re-mixed with air (the animation shows the separation and remixing).",
